//! The internal family mark — the kernel's query vocabulary written as
//! DECLARATIONS, so `collect enum` can mint `Family` from them.
//!
//! A MARK, never a second query engine: the kernel's own registration
//! stays where it is until every family has a declaration. A family
//! declaration carries the key it is addressed by and the answer it
//! holds; its NAME is its identity, so declaration order is free.
//!
//! THE LAYER SPLIT: this mark is COMPILER-INTERNAL. It is NOT
//! @std.relation's user-facing `@query fn q(db, …)`, which wraps a fn
//! whose answer carries a stable encoding — the families answer dense
//! structural values (`Parsed`, `TypeFacts`, `Unit`), carry no `Db`
//! seat, and several are inputs or whole-program fixpoints, so they
//! cannot wear that form. Neither mark weakens the other.
//!
//! Stands ALONE with @std/meta: a derive's file names nothing the
//! annotated file declares.
use @std.meta.{Named}

export fn family(_t: Named, _key: string, _answer: string) {}
